  "note": "Election of the Warrenpoint Urban District Council, 18 September 1946. There were 18 candidates for the 12 seats. East Ward (5 seats) and West Ward (7 seats) were both polled; the Belfast News-Letter printed only the elected, and the Newry Telegraph (21 September 1946, p. 6) the full poll of both wards. Labour had a majority of two on the new council; Edward Caulfield, the retiring chairman (an Independent in the Newry Telegraph, N. in the News-Letter), was defeated in the West Ward.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of Belfast News-Letter, 20 September 1946, p. 3 (council-audit, Nov 2026): the note's '15 seats' -> '12 seats', as printed; names and votes confirmed. Corrected from the page image of the Newry Telegraph, 21 September 1946, p. 6 (w8-review, Nov 2026): the five defeated candidates are added with their votes, Edward Caulfield (Ind.) 121, John Patton (U.) 120, Samuel Colvin (U.) 119, Wm. James Hourican (Ind.) 99 and Benedict Malocca (Ind.) 76, with the 431 votes cast including 7 spoiled papers; the seven elected and their figures agree."
